    "question": {
      ":question/id": "44f4f65c-c394-5e85-92b2-88eebd3326dc",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 6 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 6 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z&=-2 \\\\ y+2z&=-6 \\\\ z&=-2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-2 \\\\ y&=-6-(2)(-2)=-2 \\\\ x&=-2-(-2)(-2)-(2)(-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -2,-2,-2\\rangle$.",
