    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e6e99a08-cdaf-5e6f-82dd-2a007e322fb1",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-1R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z&=-3 \\\\ y&=-1 \\\\ z&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-4 \\\\ y&=-1-(0)(-4)=-1 \\\\ x&=-3-(1)(-1)-(2)(-4)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 6,-1,-4\\rangle$.",
