    "question": {
      ":question/id": "61742d4d-f50c-53f6-8f65-c59bfa085c8a",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-2z&=1 \\\\ y+2z&=-2 \\\\ z&=3\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=3 \\\\ y&=-2-(2)(3)=-8 \\\\ x&=1-(-1)(-8)-(-2)(3)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -1,-8,3\\rangle$.",
