    "question": {
      ":question/id": "593da203-f82a-5a4d-ac00-923d7df64cc1",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y&=0 \\\\ y-z&=3 \\\\ z&=-2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-2 \\\\ y&=3-(-1)(-2)=1 \\\\ x&=0-(2)(1)-(0)(-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -2,1,-2\\rangle$.",
