    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d620ed91-186c-5dad-a078-85246e1e4040",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z&=-4 \\\\ -x-y+3z&=-1 \\\\ -x-4y-5z&=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z&=-2 \\\\ y+2z&=-3 \\\\ z&=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=4 \\\\ y&=-3-(2)(4)=-11 \\\\ x&=-2-(2)(-11)-(-1)(4)=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 24,-11,4\\rangle$.",
